corrected_content.problem:
Evaluate $$
{\int }_{C}\mathbf{F}\cdot \text{d}\mathbf{r}
$$ given that $\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=x\hspace{0.167em}\mathbf{i}+y\hspace{0.167em}\mathbf{j}+z\hspace{0.167em}\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\mathbf{r}(t)=\operatorname{cos}t\hspace{0.167em}\mathbf{i}+\operatorname{sin}t\hspace{0.167em}\mathbf{j}+2\sqrt{t}\hspace{0.167em}\mathbf{k}$ for $t ∈ [0, π]$.
